\DOC LOCAL_MOD_P521_SAFETY_TAC

\TYPE {LOCAL_MOD_P521_SAFETY_TAC : string -> int -> tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Discharges a subroutine call inside an {eventually} goal by applying a named
assumed safety specification, advancing the symbolic state from the call site
to the state just after the call returns.

\DESCRIBE
{assump_name : string} names the assumption in the goal's assumption list that
holds the callee's {ensures} safety specification to be used; {n : int} is the
index of the current symbolic state, from which the name of the successor state
introduced for the post-call state is formed.
{
   A ?- eventually ... s_n
   ========================================  LOCAL_MOD_P521_SAFETY_TAC assump_name n
   A' ?- eventually ... s_{n+1}
}
\noindent Here {A'} is {A} with the assumptions describing the state at the
call site — program-counter, stack-pointer, argument-register and
return-address reads, the accumulated event trace, and the {MAYCHANGE} relation
from the initial state — removed and replaced by the corresponding facts about
the successor state: the restored program counter and stack pointer, an
extended event trace built from the callee's trace function, a fresh event-list
variable together with its defining equation and a {memaccess_inbounds} fact
about it, the surviving register/memory reads, and a {MAYCHANGE} relation
extended with the memory regions the callee may write. The named specification
assumption is retained, though it may be reordered within the assumption list.

\COMMENTS
The observed traces show only this single kind of transformation, always on
goals of this {eventually} shape with the callee specification present among
the assumptions.

\ENDDOC
